# Who gets asked to review what.
#
# GitHub reads this file top to bottom and the LAST matching pattern wins, which is the opposite
# of .gitignore and catches everybody once. So the catch all goes first and the paths that deserve
# more care go after it. Reordering this file changes who gets requested.
#
# Right now every line names the same person, so none of this changes who reviews anything today.
# It is written out anyway for two reasons. The paths below are the ones where a second reviewer
# should be added first when there is one, and listing them means that addition is a one line
# change rather than an argument about which files matter. And an explicit entry cannot be
# silently captured by a broader rule somebody adds later.

# Everything, unless something below is more specific.
*                                   @dotmantissa

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contract sources. Code that gets deployed and then cannot be edited.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The Stellar side. hyperion-core is listed separately below because it is the shared one.
/soroban/crates/                    @dotmantissa

# The shared primitives: decimal conversion, strkey encoding, flow accounting, error codes. Every
# other crate depends on this one, so a change here is a change to every rail at once.
/soroban/crates/hyperion-core/      @dotmantissa

# The EVM side.
/evm/src/                           @dotmantissa

# The router is where every routing decision actually lives. Nothing in this repository has a
# wider blast radius.
/evm/src/HyperionRouter.sol         @dotmantissa

# The rail adapters. Each one is the boundary between code written here and a rail nobody here
# controls, which makes them the files where a wrong assumption is most expensive.
/evm/src/adapters/                  @dotmantissa

# The shared libraries. Amount maths, flow windows, note layout, strkey encoding. These are the
# Solidity halves of the pairs that packages/protocol/test/parity.test.ts checks against the Rust,
# so a change here is almost never a change to one file.
/evm/src/libraries/                 @dotmantissa

# Error declarations and the types on the wire. The ORDER of the declarations in HyperionErrors.sol
# is load bearing: the generated selector table and errors.ts both follow it, and reordering it
# relabels every failure the contracts have ever emitted, each one plausibly.
/evm/src/HyperionErrors.sol         @dotmantissa
/evm/src/HyperionTypes.sol          @dotmantissa

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployment. Code that runs once, with a key, against something real.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The two phase timelocked deployment, the verifier and the smoke test. A mistake in phase one is
# a mistake you find out about an hour later, on a chain where the fix also takes an hour.
/evm/script/                        @dotmantissa

# The Stellar deploy scripts and the anvil rehearsal. lib.sh in particular decides how the signing
# identity is resolved, and the rule it enforces, that a named identity is used and never a secret
# read out of the environment, is the reason no key has ever reached a log here.
/script/                            @dotmantissa

# Deployment records. These are what phase two reads back and what the verifier compares the chain
# against, so an edit here can make a correct chain look wrong or a wrong chain look correct.
/deployments/                       @dotmantissa
/evm/deployments/                   @dotmantissa

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated files, build configuration, and the pins that make a build reproducible.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Generated from the Foundry build by packages/protocol/scripts/gen-artifacts.mjs. A hand edit
# here is a failing parity test, and is meant to be.
/packages/protocol/src/abi/         @dotmantissa

# The compiler settings, the fuzzer budget, the lint exclusions and the formatter rules. Changing
# optimizer_runs or via_ir changes the bytecode that ships.
/evm/foundry.toml                   @dotmantissa

# The Rust workspace, the release profile, and the toolchain pin. opt-level = "z", lto and
# panic = "abort" are all there because the wasm has to fit in 64KB.
/soroban/Cargo.toml                 @dotmantissa
/soroban/rust-toolchain.toml        @dotmantissa

# Lockfiles. What CI installs is what was tested, and that is only true while these are honest.
/soroban/Cargo.lock                 @dotmantissa
/evm/package-lock.json              @dotmantissa
/packages/protocol/package-lock.json @dotmantissa

# forge-std and OpenZeppelin are committed submodules, pinned to the revisions the suite was run
# against. Moving either one moves the ground under every test.
/.gitmodules                        @dotmantissa
/evm/lib/                           @dotmantissa

# The install flags. .npmrc carries legacy-peer-deps with a written reason, and removing it breaks
# the install outright rather than degrading it.
/packages/protocol/.npmrc           @dotmantissa

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CI and policy. A workflow can read the repository and runs on a pull request, so a change here
# is a change to the trust boundary of the build.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

/.github/                           @dotmantissa
/.github/workflows/                 @dotmantissa
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @dotmantissa
/.github/SECURITY.md                @dotmantissa

# Contribution supply chain and deployment trust boundaries.
/package.json                       @dotmantissa
/package-lock.json                  @dotmantissa
/.npmrc                             @dotmantissa
/hyperion-protocol-*.tgz             @dotmantissa
/deployments/                       @dotmantissa
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @dotmantissa

/packages/protocol/                 @dotmantissa
/evm/package*.json                  @dotmantissa
/evm/.npmrc                         @dotmantissa
/.gitmodules                       @dotmantissa
/soroban/Cargo.*                    @dotmantissa
/soroban/vendor/                    @dotmantissa
/soroban/rust-toolchain.toml         @dotmantissa
/script/                           @dotmantissa
